Upgrade = repoint HELIX_IMAGE env to v2, then `podman-compose up -d`.

## OBSERVED podman-compose divergence from docker-compose
`podman-compose up -d` recreated ALL THREE containers on upgrade (postgres/redis included, not only the
changed helix service). No data loss (named volumes survive recreation) and migrations were not re-run
(helix_schema_migrations still exactly version 1), but docker-compose would recreate only the changed
service. podman-compose also recreated containers even when nothing changed (rollback ran clean again).
Also observed: podman-compose `config` prints fully resolved secrets to stdout (docker-compose masks
nothing either, but treat `config` output as sensitive); top-level `name:` in the compose file beat
`-p helixqual-deploy` in podman-compose, so deploy/docker-compose.yml now interpolates
`name: ${COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME:-helix}` to keep isolated runs prefixable.

